hadiths[4]{hadithnumber,text}:
"328","On the authority of Bandar bin Bashar, on the authority of Muhammad bin Jaafar, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Al-Muhajir Abi Al-Hasan, that he heard Zaid bin Wahb speaking to him, on the authority of Abu Dhar, he said: The muezzin of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, called the call to prayer at noon, and the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “It gets colder, it gets colder,” or he said: Wait, wait.” He said: “The intensity of the heat is a result of the stench of Hell, so when the heat becomes intense, cool off with prayer.” Abu Dharr said: Until we saw the sky above the hills."
"329","Abdul-Jabbar bin Al-Ala’, Sa’id bin Abdul-Rahman Al-Makhzoumi, and Ahmad bin Abda Al-Dhabi told us, they said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Sa`id, who is Ibn al-Musayyab, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “When the heat becomes intense, cool off.” Prayer, for the intensity of the heat is from the blazing heat of Hell.”"
"330","Bindar bin Bashar told us, Abdul Wahhab told us, meaning Al-Thaqafi, Ubaid Allah bin Omar told us, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Omar, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him. He, peace and blessings be upon him, said: “Indeed, the intensity of the heat is a result of the blazing heat of Hell, so cool the prayer during the intensity of the heat.”"
"331","Al-Qasim bin Muhammad bin Abbad Al-Muhallabi, on the authority of Abdullah, meaning Ibn Dawud Al-Khuraibi, on the authority of Hisham bin Urwa, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Aisha, may God Almighty be pleased with her, said that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Cool the afternoon heat in the heat.”"
